1:1 COMMENT "# generator_accepts_borrow.z -- a generator whose per-call input is"
1:68 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# a borrowed reftype."
2:22 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "#"
3:2 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# `call: function {bag: Bag.borrow}` makes each `.call bag: b`"
4:63 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# deposit a borrowed pointer to the caller's Bag into the"
5:58 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# generator's resume slot. The lock is held for the duration of the"
6:68 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# call; on resumption, `name: yield v` binds `name` as a pointer"
7:65 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# alias into the caller's storage, so `name.x` reads the LIVE field"
8:68 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# through the lock."
9:20 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "#"
10:2 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "# Liveness rule: `name` is valid only until the NEXT yield. Using it"
11:69 EOL "\n"
12:1 COMMENT "# past that point would read a different `.call`'s caller storage"
12:66 EOL "\n"
13:1 COMMENT "# (or stale data on a follow-up resumption). The typechecker rejects"
13:69 EOL "\n"
14:1 COMMENT "# such uses with a hint pointing at `.take` for the"
14:52 EOL "\n"
15:1 COMMENT "# store-across-yields case."
15:28 EOL "\n"
16:1 COMMENT "#"
16:2 EOL "\n"
17:1 COMMENT "# The label is the author's: `bag:` here is what the call sites"
17:64 EOL "\n"
18:1 COMMENT "# read, and nothing in the compiler requires it to be spelled"
18:62 EOL "\n"
19:1 COMMENT "# `value`."
19:11 EOL "\n"
20:1 EOL "\n"
21:1 LABEL "Bag"
21:4 COLON ":"
21:5 WS " "
21:6 CLASS "class"
21:11 WS " "
21:12 BRACEOPEN "{"
21:13 EOL "\n"
22:1 WS "    "
22:5 LABEL "x"
22:6 COLON ":"
22:7 WS " "
22:8 REFID "i64"
22:11 EOL "\n"
23:1 BRACECLOSE "}"
23:2 EOL "\n"
24:1 EOL "\n"
25:1 COMMENT "# Three-yield generator: emits 1, then reads the resumed bag's x"
25:65 EOL "\n"
26:1 COMMENT "# field. `b` is used in the same window it was bound in (between"
26:65 EOL "\n"
27:1 COMMENT "# `b: yield 2` and the next `yield`), so the liveness check passes."
27:68 EOL "\n"
